 "notes": [
  "Two-card tier throughout: physical npu:2,npu:3 (logical npu:0,npu:1). The tier is 996 slots for the serve runs and 1057 for the graphs-off GSM8K arm - not the four-card 2480-slot tier the committed numbers used, so tok/s is not comparable across card counts; accuracy and answers are.",
  "Page cache was warm for every run: read_bytes was 0.06 GB (gsm8k off), 0.16-0.88 GB (sustained), 1.36 GB (multi-turn) and 1.74 GB (gsm8k on) against 1.2-7.8 TB of rchar. These are warm-array numbers.",
  "The multi-turn run passed --turn-suffix-tokens 80, but the harness at the time sliced suffix_n+gen = 112 tokens per turn; the code now takes exactly suffix_n. The measured run's per-turn rows carry the true 112 fresh tokens (prompt grows by 144 = 112 + 32 gen per turn, 512 -> 1808).",
  "Sustained run A was recorded before the harness read graph_captures and decode_tok_s into its summary; its engine log says 'graphs captured 98 in 4677 ms' (the 4.84 s max interval) and its rate is 220 tokens / 172.83 s = 1.27 tok/s. Run B records both fields directly.",
  "The graph capture is charged to one decode step, so the single largest interval in each sustained run (4.84 s / 5.02 s) is the capture, not a slow token; excluding it the max step was 1.03 s.",
  "The working tree also carries another agent's uncommitted EP edits (model.py/parallel.py). Its paths are gated on ep_size>1, which is 1 on the single-rank path every run here takes; bench_serve.py and eval_gsm8k.py are the only files this measurement edited."
 ]
}